WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.467
Your first real send went out
because a second person approved it.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:06.767
Now decide who that person is,
and what everyone else can touch.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:10.067
Get it right once, and nobody
can widen their own reach.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.067
In this clip you'll know
how members, role profiles,

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:15.300
delegations and agent keys fit together,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.700
and what stops anyone
from locking you out.

00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:21.400
Leo hands Orbit a full access key in
March and never looks at it again.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.200
By June an agency still has access,
three people share one login,

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.033
and the access list has no owner.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.733
Reach should be given
on purpose, and checked.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.267
First, members, because every
other control hangs off a role.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:36.700
Invite people by email and give
each one owner, admin or member.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.133
In the console: Settings, Members.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.533
Or ask your agent: "Who is on the
team and what can each role do".

00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:46.033
Only owners and admins approve,
and nobody approves their own work.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.667
A builder role exists
for delegated agencies,

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.900
and a service role for system accounts.

00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:54.333
Second, role profiles, which
turn a role into a seat.

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:57.533
The built in ones are Operator,
Ops lead, Exec and Engineer,

00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:01.867
and Exec is an admin without configuration, journey and send operations.

00:01:01.867 --> 00:01:06.033
Add your own with a base role,
the operations it can never use,

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.533
and the tiles and actions it sees first.

00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:11.033
A profile can only narrow
a role, never widen it.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.100
Each profile has a seat dashboard,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.967
so people open GTM OS on
the work that's theirs.

00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:18.933
Ask your agent: "What does
my seat dashboard show".

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:20.867
A member's agents inherit the seat.

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:24.733
So an agent working for an Exec
can't send what the Exec can't send.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.333
Assigning a seat is human only. Ask
your agent: "Make Priya an Ops lead",

00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:33.833
and it names the screen and the button
instead: Settings, Members, Profile.

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.300
Power habit: put executives
on the Exec profile,

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.167
so they see the numbers and can't
change configuration or send.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.300
Third, agencies, which
work through delegations.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.633
Your owner or admin grants an
agency organization access,

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:49.733
and the grant stays pending until
an owner or admin approves it.

00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:52.700
The agency acts as a
builder, never an owner,

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.200
so it can build but can't
approve its own work.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.133
In the console: Settings, Delegations.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.500
Or ask your agent: "Which agencies
have access to our organization".

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.067
Revoking takes two clicks, and the
agency loses access on its next request.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.533
Fourth, sign in and keys.
Signup can be closed.

00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:13.233
Invitations bring people in, and
an allow list limits who can join.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.567
Google, Microsoft or your
own SSO can handle the login.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.533
Setting up SSO is human only,

00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:21.200
so an agent can't point
your login at a provider.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:23.767
Agent keys connect Claude Code or Codex.

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.967
In the console: Settings, Developer.

00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:31.033
Pick a preset, full GTM engineer, read
write or read only, and an expiry,

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.133
ninety days by default.
The key is shown once.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:36.167
Or ask your agent: "Create
an agent key for Sam",

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.300
and it points you to that screen.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:43.033
Operator tip: give an agent the read
only preset until a job needs more.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.767
Last, the guard under all of it.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:48.000
An organization must always
keep someone who can repair it.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.867
Removing the last owner, or narrowing
a role so nobody can finish setup,

00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:56.000
is refused. And a profile can never
deny the role operations themselves,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.733
so you can always fix a
profile that went too far.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.033
The skeptic's line: an agent
key is a back door. It isn't.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:05.733
A key's reach is the overlap of
its own scopes, the agent's scopes,

00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:08.267
and the current role of
the person who made it.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.433
Demote that person, and
their keys shrink too.

00:03:10.433 --> 00:03:14.467
A key never gets the approve permission,
and it can't create another key.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:18.633
The person who created it can't approve
what it proposes. And it expires.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:22.033
Every role change, delegation
and key lands in the audit log,

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:25.367
under Settings, Audit log.
A review reads from fact.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.867
Approvals, Safety and your
dashboards all follow the seat.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.200
One limit to plan for.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.800
A key never approves, and neither
does the person behind it.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.733
So a team of one still needs a
second person, or a second identity,

00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:38.400
as approver.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:42.433
In one pass: Members get roles,
profiles narrow roles into seats,

00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:44.967
agencies come in by
delegation, and keys expire.

00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:49.333
Everyone gets the reach they were
given, and nobody can widen their own.

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:53.167
Your team has the reach it needs
and no more, your agents inherit it,

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:55.500
and the organization
can always be repaired.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.067
Next up, Tutorial: your first month,

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.433
where you read the results
and tune from them.
